generatedCommentsNodes.comment:
The `dataType` field in `StEnvelope` is only assigned inside `resolveType()`, but it is not serialized in the `StreamInput` constructor. After deserialization (e.g., in a distributed execution plan), `dataType()` will return `null` because `resolveType()` has not been re-invoked. Compare with `StXMax`/`StXMin`/`StYMax`/`StYMin`, which always return the constant `DOUBLE`. A safe fix is to compute the return type directly in `dataType()` from the field's type:
```java
@Override
public DataType dataType() {
    return switch (field().dataType()) {
        case GEO_POINT, GEO_SHAPE -> GEO_SHAPE;
        case CARTESIAN_POINT, CARTESIAN_SHAPE -> CARTESIAN_SHAPE;
        default -> NULL;
    };
}
```
This eliminates the mutable field entirely and makes the class safe across serialization boundaries.

